From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 23:50:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] JavaScriptCore: one GC marker on the 68k

reddit's reCAPTCHA worker lost a live object's Structure: the object kept
a Structure the last collection had not marked, the next property
transition reused that cell for the new Structure (previous == this), and
the worker aborted (and sometimes the page waited for it for ever). It
was timing dependent: 3 of 20 runs on an idle Instance-32, none under host
load. With numberOfGCMarkers=1 and useParallelMarkingConstraintSolver=false
it was 0 of 30 on the same binary.

A 68040 has one core, so the helper markers only take turns with the main
one. overrideDefaults() now sets one marker and the serial constraint
solver on CPU(M68K); OBJSC can still set either.

Team 3
---
diff --git a/Source/JavaScriptCore/runtime/Options.cpp b/Source/JavaScriptCore/runtime/Options.cpp
index 3ef49ba..ec334bf 100644
--- a/Source/JavaScriptCore/runtime/Options.cpp
+++ b/Source/JavaScriptCore/runtime/Options.cpp
@@ -574,6 +574,16 @@ static unsigned numberOfSuperAndPerformanceCores()
 
 static void overrideDefaults()
 {
+#if CPU(M68K)
+    // One marker. Helper markers race the worker's own marking on the 68k:
+    // reddit's reCAPTCHA worker lost a live object's Structure (the next
+    // transition reused its cell, previous == this) in 3 of 20 runs with the
+    // default markers and 0 of 30 with one. A 68040 has one core, so helper
+    // markers only take turns with the main one. OBJSC can still set both.
+    Options::numberOfGCMarkers() = 1;
+    Options::useParallelMarkingConstraintSolver() = false;
+#endif
+
 #if OS(DARWIN)
     if (Options::machExceptionHandlerSandboxPolicy == Options::SandboxPolicy::Block)
         disableAllSignalHandlerBasedOptions();
